A||N||9||Dan87GT||New V6 engine won't start||||1||
Z||000000||Dan87GT||09-22-2001||08:10 PM||||I just got done installing a rebuilt 2.8 in my 86SE, I can't get the thing to start. I am getting spark and fuel. I just hear random firing. I also made sure I had the distributor in right. If I floor the pedal, I get a little more backfiring. Any thoughts????||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-22-2001||08:22 PM||||Had the same problem with my rebuilt engine.  Make sure you the distributor is installed correctly and adjust it so that at top dead center the rotor points to the #1 terminal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||86seyellow||09-22-2001||08:22 PM||||Did you check to see if the fuel rail is getting pressure?? WHen I had mine done, just got it back, we replaced all the injectors.<BR><P>------------------<BR>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||Spektrum-87GT||09-22-2001||10:11 PM||||as funny as this may sound... did you hook back up the computer?||||reg||1
Z||000004||JetroGT||09-23-2001||04:21 AM||||I had the same problem when I went to rebuild my V6. I did the top dead center thing. But the cylinder was on the wrong stroke. I just turned the rotor 180, and it started up.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg"> <P>I work where all the missing paperclips go.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan87GT||09-24-2001||08:20 AM||||As a follow-up, I rechecked the rotor and top-dead center. I did find that the cold-start valve was leaking at the fuel rail. After all that it still won't start, I still can't figure out why it sputters when I floor the gas and doesn't do anything when the pedal is up..Any other thoughts??? ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Indiana_resto_guy||09-24-2001||09:17 AM||||Are you using the correct timing mark?<BR>There are three cuts across the balancer, you want to use the widest. Also are you sure that #1 cylinder is on the compression stroke?||||reg||1
Z||000007||87GTZ34||09-24-2001||09:51 AM||||Dan,<BR>  It is possible that the marks you are using on the harmonic balancer are incorrect.  A previous owner may have replaced it (not for a Fiero but a 60 degree V6) or that the outer ring shifted from the 'correct' position so timing the car using that timing mark is impossible. To check it, use a new/clean drinking staw in #1 cylinder (thru the plug hole), rotate to TDC using the straw (watch for the highest point) and then note the markings on the balancer. You symptom really sounds alot like timing or firing order problems.  GL<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 09-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Back On Holiday||09-25-2001||12:38 AM||||I am having the same problem.  I will be taking all the advice into the garage tomorrow night to see if it works.  Just curious to the original poster, did you get it to start yet?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero_Freak||09-25-2001||07:49 AM||||I pulled a valve cover and watched the rocker arms to find the correct timing mark.  I too was using the wrong one.....FOR TWO DAMN DAYS!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
